    "field": "Aerosol-cloud interactions",
    "problem": "Accurately quantifying aerosol-cloud radiative forcing, the largest uncertainty in climate change projections, is challenging because cloud responses to aerosols are complexly governed by co-varying meteorological conditions and precipitation states that are difficult to isolate and analyze using traditional satellite observations.",
    "method": "This paper presents a method to quantify aerosol-cloud radiative forcing by analyzing co-located observations of aerosols and single-layer marine warm clouds from multiple A-Train satellites, considering the governing effects of tropospheric stability, free-tropospheric humidity, and the state of precipitation on cloud responses.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the global aerosol-cloud radiative forcing by marine warm clouds through a comprehensive analysis of co-located aerosol and cloud observations from multiple Earth-observing satellites.",
