            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "marine AOD parameterization",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "MACC is a framework developed by ECMWF Integrated Forecast System, and is the first aerosol model fully coupled to a numerical weather prediction model with data assimilation of satellite aerosol optical depth28. Different aerosol species (sea salt, dust, organic matter, black carbon, and sulphate) are included in MACC. To calculate the anthropogenic aerosol fraction, we follow the algorithms as in ref. 19, in which aerosols are separated into marine, dust, and anthropogenic. Here, marine AOD is a function of ECMWF wind speed, w (that is, AOD marine =0.006w+0.06). Applying the same algorithms, we identify the global anthropogenic aerosol distribution (Supplementary Fig. 1).",
